Package: google-photos-auto-compressor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Reyfen <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Reyfen/GooglePhotosAutoCompressor
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.27), libgcc-s1 | libgcc1, libstdc++6, zlib1g, libssl3 | libssl3t64 | libssl1.1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libx11-6, libice6, libsm6, libxext6, libxrandr2, libxi6, libxcursor1
Recommends: ffmpeg
Suggests: google-chrome-stable
Description: Free up Google Photos storage by compressing big videos and photos
 Opens Google Photos in Chrome, downloads the largest videos and photos,
 makes smaller copies (ffmpeg for video, JPEG for photos), checks them,
 moves the originals to the Google Photos bin and uploads the copies with
 their original dates. Stops and resumes safely at any point.
